    "OtherAbstract": {
      "Type": "PIP",
      "Language": "eng",
      "AbstractText": "530 patients were reviewed 6 months following laparoscopic sterilization by diathermy (235 patients) or silastic bands (295 patients). Particular focus was on menstrual and sexual problems 6 months after the operation. The mean age of the patients was 34.1 years, and the mean parity was 2.3. At 6 months there had been 2 failures in the silastic band group and 1 in the diathermy group. When the 2 methods were compared, there were no differences in the nature or incidence of menstrual problems. 40% of all patients reported an increase in menstrual loss. 26% of the patients reported an increase in menstrual pain, and this could not be attributed totally to the stopping of oral contraception. 42% of the patients indicated an improvement in their sex lives after sterilization, while 6.6% reported deterioration primarily because of lack of libido. 5.1% of the patients expressed some regret about the operation."
    }
